er-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "76df303e-8d36-5a1a-a707-d9f9700fcc81" :question/math-academy-id "q-97146" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.64),$ compute $P(X<5).$  Round your final answer to $4$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.64),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{(0.36)}^{x-1}(0.64), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in {1,2,3,4}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & ={(0.36)}^{0}(0.64)+{(0.36)}^{1}(0.64)+{(0.36)}^{2}(0.64)+{(0.36)}^{3}(0.64) \\\\  & ≈0.9832.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363418 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c566525f-9b0f-586f-ba60-277400cb25dd" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over a Bounded Interval: Lower Bound is Not Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac6cc09c-cf9b-5297-b361-cf0a60736014" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4166" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363420} {:answer/id #uuid "b08e5362-3274-52f3-b344-9f9fc1de0fcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2287" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363421} {:answer/id #uuid "143b8ba4-fc16-53be-944e-a2c09f494df8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2481" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363422} {:answer/id #uuid "aa3a3511-f240-55a8-a5b7-03a6d6eb93c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3258" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363423} {:answer/id #uuid "491dae5e-a6ff-583f-8c3f-4084a8a26478" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3004" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "143b8ba4-fc16-53be-944e-a2c09f494df8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2481" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363422} :answer-field/id #uuid "b450dc1e-c7a0-5f00-b80c-6657edae450c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41ac5158-0a88-50a3-be11-7ca04a52f9cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-97155" :question/problem "Given that $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.23),$ compute $P(3<X<7)$ rounded to $4$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.23),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{(0.77)}^{x-1}(0.23), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3<X<7) & =P(X\\in {4,5,6}) \\\\  & =P(X=4)+P(X=5)+P(X=6) \\\\  & =f(4)+f(5)+f(6) \\\\  & ={(0.77)}^{3}(0.23)+{(0.77)}^{4}(0.23)+{(0.77)}^{5}(0.23) \\\\  & ≈0.2481.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363425 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "215130d1-96ea-5f88-8de0-d73758ea8344" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over a Bounded Interval Using the Complement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d49af3ed-e963-5844-8f75-83a434537a1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.973" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363427} {:answer/id #uuid "1841346a-4636-586d-9b64-9994661d90e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.027" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363428} {:answer/id #uuid "c494f012-1182-5589-8e43-bd03f8ad97b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.908" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363429} {:answer/id #uuid "58749640-ef45-5d6a-a47d-7e8477253484" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.932" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363430} {:answer/id #uuid "3915a24f-698e-5442-9422-3d61dea6ce0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.092" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1841346a-4636-586d-9b64-9994661d90e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.027" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363428} :answer-field/id #uuid "a754b1a4-788e-5709-8a0e-9d1d9dba3b84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363426}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0f41b6a4-50b1-5122-8260-283c4994a71d" :question/math-academy-id "q-97176" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.7),$ compute $P(X>3).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.7),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{(0.3)}^{x-1}(0.7), & x=1,2,3… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are infinitely many values of $X$ such that $X>3.$ However, we can simplify the computation by using the complement instead:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>3) & =1-P(X\\le 3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =P(X\\in {1,2,3}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & ={(0.3)}^{0}(0.7)+{(0.3)}^{1}(0.7)+{(0.3)}^{2}(0.7) \\\\  & =0.973.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>3) & =1-P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =1-0.973 \\\\  & =0.027.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363432 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "215130d1-96ea-5f88-8de0-d73758ea8344" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over a Bounded Interval Using the Complement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15694b94-1937-5244-a027-11fe5c4274c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.612" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363434} {:answer/id #uuid "f929f937-8fd5-526c-b2c5-d85f9d689615" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.284" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363435} {:answer/id #uuid "62bce381-b641-5c0d-be81-17ccada1b3da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.216" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363436} {:answer/id #uuid "78841346-e150-54e8-94ca-78393f54c53b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.784" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363437} {:answer/id #uuid "50c01ca3-49bc-5bd2-a61f-68ce9602af6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.716" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62bce381-b641-5c0d-be81-17ccada1b3da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.216" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363436} :answer-field/id #uuid "fac21599-cb2a-5939-89ed-58b73f529127" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363433}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "688411cb-4042-5ded-9f38-8c3face1b1ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-97178" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.4),$ compute $P(X\\ge 4)$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.4),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{(0.6)}^{x-1}(0.4), & x=1,2,3… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are infinitely many values of $X$ such that $X\\ge 4.$ However, we can simplify the computation by using the complement instead:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 4) & =1-P(X<4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<4) & =P(X\\in {1,2,3}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & ={(0.6)}^{0}(0.4)+{(0.6)}^{1}(0.4)+{(0.6)}^{2}(0.4) \\\\  & =0.784.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 4) & =1-P(X<4) \\\\  & =1-0.784 \\\\  & =0.216.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
